WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:03.240
Buzzy HBO shows, Universal monster movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:09.231
and an unusual Suicide Squad role. It's obvious&nbsp;
why Riley in "The Last of Us" looks so familiar.

00:00:09.231 --> 00:00:13.260
In Season 1, Episode 6 of HBO's "The&nbsp;
Last of Us," Joel ends up taking a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:16.800
nasty piece of wood to the abdomen, and&nbsp;
Ellie wonders if her newly adopted father&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:20.460
will survive. Judging by almost every&nbsp;
encounter the duo has had in the past,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:24.960
the odds don't exactly look good in Ellie's&nbsp;
eyes. Basically, if there was ever a time for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:28.380
a reprieve from the relentlessness of&nbsp;
"The Last of Us," that moment is now.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:31.200
Giving the audience a breather&nbsp;
from Joel's harrowing present,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:36.360
Episode 7 tells Ellie's backstory. Raised in the&nbsp;
FEDRA run military school, there's little room for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:40.620
freedom. However, Ellie does form a friendship&nbsp;
with another student named Riley – who ends up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:44.700
leaving her to join the Fireflies. While the&nbsp;
Fireflies are dubbed a terrorist organization,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:49.560
Riley is important to Ellie. In this world,&nbsp;
friends are few and far between. Unsurprisingly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:53.280
a young actor who has already appeared in&nbsp;
many high-profile projects was selected to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:55.980
take on one of the most important&nbsp;
roles in "The Last of Us" so far.

00:00:56.191 --> 00:00:58.171
"Well I appreciate your mercy."

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:03.000
As a child, Storm Reid was no stranger to acting,&nbsp;
but it was her leading role in "A Wrinkle In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:07.560
Time" which set her up for success, and saw her&nbsp;
starring alongside Chris Pine, Oprah Winfrey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:11.820
Reese Witherspoon, and Mindy Kaling. "A Wrinkle&nbsp;
In Time" is known to many because it is based&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:16.620
on a classic science fiction children's book.&nbsp;
Written in the 1960s by Madeleine L’Engle, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:20.280
story was the start of a five-book series about&nbsp;
Meg Murry and the search for her missing father.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:24.000
2018's feature film wasn't the&nbsp;
first time the book was adapted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:28.860
but it did break many barriers in the process.&nbsp;
With "Selma" director Ava DuVernay at the helm,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:32.760
the film gives an alternate perspective to a&nbsp;
book that was released over half a century ago.

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:37.020
Casting Reid in the lead role contrasted with&nbsp;
previous adaptations, and was a significant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:40.980
step for representation. Even though DuVernay&nbsp;
theorized that not everyone would appreciate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:44.700
the casting of a young girl of color in the&nbsp;
leading role, many found merit in the final&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:49.200
product. Despite the fact that the film received&nbsp;
mixed reviews, it remains a beautiful and sweeping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:53.880
story that stays true to the book. Reid would&nbsp;
later reunite with DuVernay in 2019 for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:57.720
director's acclaimed limited series "When&nbsp;
They See Us," based on the tragedy of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:02.744
Central Park Five. In that project, she played&nbsp;
Lisa, the real-life girlfriend of Korey Wise.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:07.620
The Universal Monster universe never really took&nbsp;
off, but Leigh Whannell deserves respect for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:11.760
his updated version of classic movie "The&nbsp;
Invisible Man." Starring Elisabeth Moss,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:16.140
the 2020 film follows one woman's attempts to&nbsp;
rid herself of abusive ex-boyfriend Adrian,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:18.000
who just so happens to be a tech genius.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:22.680
The insidious abuse that Cecilia experienced&nbsp;
during their relationship was so severe that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:25.740
she doesn't believe it when she's told&nbsp;
that Adrian has died from suicide.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:29.400
Unfortunately for her and those around&nbsp;
her, she is proven right when Adrian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:33.300
resurfaces with technology that allows&nbsp;
him to be invisible. Everyone suffers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:37.080
especially Sydney, played by Storm Reid,&nbsp;
the daughter of Cecilia's friend James.

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:42.600
Adrian hits Sydney when only Cecilia is in the&nbsp;
room, framing her for the attack. Sydney is the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:46.800
ultimate innocent in the situation, unable&nbsp;
to understand what happened to her. Cecilia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:50.700
eventually gets the better of her ex at the end&nbsp;
of "The Invisible Man," but not before so much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:55.020
damage is done. Reid doesn't have a large amount&nbsp;
of screen time, but she does exemplary work,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:58.980
and displays heartbreaking emotion in one of the&nbsp;
most uncomfortable scenes in the entire movie.

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:05.160
DC's 2021 reboot of 2016's "Suicide Squad"&nbsp;
came with many surprises, both delightful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:09.480
and heartwrenching. After his Marvel tenure,&nbsp;
James Gunn arrived in the director's chair to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:13.200
keep what worked from the previous film and&nbsp;
set everything else on fire. In a wise move,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:17.820
he kept Margot Robbieas Harley Quinn and Joel&nbsp;
Kinnaman as Rick Flagg for an all-new adventure.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:22.080
Opting to remove Jared Leto's Joker and the&nbsp;
character's controversial relationship with Harley&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:26.834
from "The Suicide Squad," Gunn instead decided to&nbsp;
tell a universal story about the power of family.

00:03:26.834 --> 00:03:28.214
"We're all going to die."

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:30.120
"I hope so."

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:33.780
At the center of this story is&nbsp;
Bloodsport, played by Idris Elba,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:37.860
who is in prison for trying to kill Superman.&nbsp;
As if that wasn't enough to prove he's no hero,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:41.400
he also happens to be a terrible father.&nbsp;
Because of his past with his own father,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:45.900
Bloodsport pushes away his daughter Tyla, who is&nbsp;
played by Reid, when she visits him in prison.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:50.400
But underneath it all, he does care for her.&nbsp;
In fact, Amanda Waller blackmails Bloodsport&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:53.760
into joining the Suicide Squad because&nbsp;
of his love for his daughter. And through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:57.942
all his trials and tribulations, he takes&nbsp;
one step closer to being a worthy father.

00:03:57.942 --> 00:04:02.580
HBO's hit teen drama "Euphoria" stars&nbsp;
Zendaya as drug-addicted high schooler Rue,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:05.700
and the series focuses on the&nbsp;
sharpest experiences of growing up.

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:09.480
"Class of '26 is like obsessed with 'Euphoria.'"

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:13.440
Relationships are at the center of the series,&nbsp;
and that includes the conflict Rue has with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:18.000
her family. In Season 2, Rue has a dramatic&nbsp;
relapse which culminates in a harrowing scene&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:22.620
between her and her sister Gia, who is played&nbsp;
by Reid. While the sisters have a profound bond,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:26.280
the foundation of their relationship is&nbsp;
shaken to its core. At such a young age,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:29.820
Reid demonstrates that she has an acting&nbsp;
range on par with her Emmy-winning co-star.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:33.660
Discussing her offscreen relationship&nbsp;
with Zendaya, Reid told Elle Australia,

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:35.880
"It's important to have some conversations and get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:38.460
to know a person before you are doing&nbsp;
these emotional scenes with a person."

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:41.160
With so many incredible&nbsp;
performances under her belt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:44.640
Reid's star is only going to rise further&nbsp;
following her appearance on "The Last of Us."

